{"agent":"bhh","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The stated failure is that a name-based knob scan treats `perf_metrics.detect_*` as dead because perfdetect reads those knobs unqualified. This edit does not change perfdetect and does not add any qualified name that was not already a load: `ring_max_bytes`, `ring_max_age_s`, `aggregate_min_samples`, and every `detect_*` attribute were already referenced as `config.perf_metrics.<knob>` and the function already returned `config.perf_metrics`. Binding the same loads to `_` and returning a prior `section` alias is invisible to that scan. Given perfdetect source that mentions `detect_min_samples` (and the other `detect_*` knobs) without a `perf_metrics.` prefix, `test_no_knob_is_dead` still fails exactly as before B61962d45e0.","digest":"d402f3265189742a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/store.py:316","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/perf/store.py:316"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The bug-fix task requires a regression test that fails on the unfixed code and is what closes B61962d45e0. The whole change is only this store.py rewrite, so nothing asserts the qualified `detect_*` names stay live. A later edit that drops the tuple (or leaves perfdetect unqualified) ships with the same dead-knob failure and no test to catch it.","digest":"30b7a557c260dfea","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/store.py:314","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/store.py:314"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"1901751590925ae5c48183a557e687db83c3d3c3","delta_raised":["d402f3265189742a","30b7a557c260dfea"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":1447,"diff_sha":"3859d9db54d4b0f897e2a2dc3c05c817382ec75f5d1837a417fe82bb5a592472","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 1901751590","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":75.9,"family":"xai",